{
  "doc": "Doc07",
  "spec": "Doc 07 T-01/T-02/FR-03 — consumer contracts for the NON-ticket events Doc 07 consumes (S07 step 3; the ticket.* slices live in fixtures/tickets/consumers/doc07.json)",
  "note": "The keys Doc 07's consumers DEPEND ON, per event. A producer removing or renaming any `reads` key breaks this document; a schema_version bump here must be reconciled deliberately (InboxEventConsumerContractsTest enforces both). channel.health.changed's entry is the event's FIRST consumer contract (inherited row 5). telegram.window.reopened's assignee_id and the bell's wider slices join at step 12 with the FR-26 fanout — noted here so the tightening is deliberate. S09 packet 2 (countersigned): the three ai.* bell arms — killswitch -> ai.killswitch holders (actor excluded), anomaly -> reports.supervisor.live holders, digest -> recipient_id only. S11 step 9 (P-C2): the two rescue arms — the projector reads ticket_id only (membership from the rescue_flags row). S12 batch D (P-CHIP, countersigned): sla.warned / sla.breached — the projector reads ticket_id only (state and due_at come from Chips::forTicket, never the payload).",
  "entries": [
    {
